WEBVTT

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:02.880
You gave an agent permission

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:03.480
to pay.

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:05.360
Then you revoked that

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:05.840
permission.

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.140
Can an approval issued earlier

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.420
still spend your funds?

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:11.760
ProofPass combines private

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.180
authorization with

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:15.020
execution-time revocation.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:17.600
This demo shows a recorded

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:18.700
testnet run.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:20.940
First,

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:22.380
the private policy.

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:25.140
Identity details and the full

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:27.200
delegation limit stay off the

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.200
destination chain.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:31.020
The public request identifies

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:33.180
the agent, recipient, and

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:33.580
amount.

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:35.780
Midnight checks identity

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:37.470
evidence from the Open D

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.160
I D SDK,

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:40.720
credential status,

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.020
wallet binding, and delegation

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:43.800
conditions.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.300
Here is why zero knowledge

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:47.680
matters.

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:50.120
The proof shows that zero

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:52.320
point zero five SOL is

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:53.780
within a hidden per-transaction

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:54.340
limit.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:56.880
The demo discloses a limit

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:58.600
of zero point one SOL

00:00:58.600 --> 00:00:59.480
for explanation.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:01.880
A request for zero point

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:03.760
one five fails before

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:05.240
authorization is created.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:08.660
Now, an actual payment.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.540
A trusted relay registers the

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:13.440
request-bound authorization on

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:13.940
Solana.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.260
The program checks the request,

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:17.260
current state,

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:19.700
expiry, and whether the approval

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:20.480
is unused.

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:23.520
Fifty million lamports move from

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:24.760
the vault to the recipient.

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:25.840
That is

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:28.290
zero point zero five test

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:28.580
SOL.

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:31.960
Here is the critical case.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:34.920
A separate, unused authorization

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.280
already exists.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:38.120
Then the X R P

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:40.260
L credential is deleted, and

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:42.000
the observer updates Solana's

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:42.260
state.

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:45.360
Executing the old approval fails

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:47.320
with source error six thousand

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:47.760
three.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:50.240
About seven seconds remain

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:51.340
before expiry.

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:54.100
Authority was revoked, so the

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:54.960
payment is blocked.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.160
No funds move from the

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:58.280
vault to the recipient.

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:01.860
Compare all four outcomes.

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:04.160
A valid request is paid.

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:06.660
Reusing the same approval is

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:07.120
rejected.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.840
Revoking the mandate blocks an

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:10.420
old approval.

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:12.980
Deleting the credential also

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.780
blocks an old approval once

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.340
the update reaches Solana.

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.140
Both successful payments and

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:21.120
rejected attempts have execution

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:21.740
evidence.

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:25.060
The trust boundaries are

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:25.520
explicit.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:28.060
Solana does not verify Midnight

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:29.120
proofs directly.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:31.540
The system trusts adapters,

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:32.440
a relay,

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:34.900
an observer, and supplied time.

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:37.500
Revocation propagation takes

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:39.580
time, and enforcement covers

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:41.100
this vault's payment path.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:44.260
Corporate agent delegation is a

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:45.200
future experiment.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:47.520
Prove permission privately.

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:49.620
Enforce it at execution.
